{"id":31118494869,"name":"Test","node_id":"WFR_kwLOA_1uaM8AAAAHPs6MlQ","head_branch":"claude/dhis2-21948-memoise-json-parse-2.43","head_sha":"76b11c399ec559a77544176335e024c03155f39d","path":".github/workflows/run-tests.yml","run_number":55462,"run_attempt":1,"event":"pull_request","display_title":"perf: parse the enrollments document once per row, not once per column [DHIS2-21948] (2.43)","status":"completed","conclusion":"failure","workflow_id":10954,"check_suite_id":84415123559,"check_suite_node_id":"CS_kwDOA_1uaM8AAAATp4iQZw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/31118494869","html_url":"https://github.com/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/31118494869","created_at":"2026-08-06T16:04:16Z","updated_at":"2026-08-06T17:18:45Z","run_started_at":"2026-08-06T16:04:16Z","jobs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/31118494869/jobs","logs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/31118494869/logs","check_suite_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/check-suites/84415123559","artifacts_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/31118494869/artifacts","cancel_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/31118494869/cancel","rerun_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/31118494869/rerun","head_commit":{"message":"perf: parse the enrollments document once per row, not once per column [DHIS2-21948] (2.43)\n\nSqlRowSetJsonExtractorDelegator deserialised the whole enrollments JSON on every\nsingle column access, from two independent call sites - getObject and\ngetRowContextItem - both of which took super.getString(\"enrollments\") and handed\nit to a fresh ObjectMapper.readValue. TrackedEntityListGrid.addNamedRows loops\ncolumns inside a loop over rows, so the count was rows x columns x 2: roughly two\nmillion parses on the trackedEntities/query export UGANDA-10 traced, and 46.8% of\nthat request's CPU. The near-even 186/190 split of profile samples between the two\ncall sites is what showed nothing was memoised.\n\nThe document is now parsed at most once per row. The memo is keyed on the document\nrather than on the cursor position, which is what makes a stale hit impossible\nrather than merely unlikely: a hit requires the current row's document to equal the\nmemoised one, and equal input cannot parse to a different result. String.equals\nshort-circuits on identity, and the identity case is the one that actually happens -\nResultSetWrappingSqlRowSet returns the same String instance for repeated reads of a\nrow, which the benchmark asserts rather than assumes.\n\nMeasured over the real row-set path (jdbcTemplate.queryForRowSet against Postgres),\n50 000 rows x 10 program-stage data-element dimensions = 1 000 000 accesses,\nthree passes after a warm-up:\n\n  before   cpu 9425 / 9804 / 9408 ms   allocated 19 239 MB\n  after    cpu  957 / 1145 / 1134 ms   allocated  2 704 MB\n\n8.6x less CPU, 7.1x less allocation, and the same values out of the grid\n(byte-identical checksum over every value and row-context item).\n\nThe new test asserts the parse count, not the wall time: four accesses over two\ncolumns must produce exactly one parse, a second row with a different document must\nre-parse, and the values and rowContext value statuses are pinned. The state added\nis per-instance on a per-request object; this class must not become shared.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e","author":{"name":"Stian Sandvold","email":"stian@dhis2.org"},"id":"76b11c399ec559a77544176335e024c03155f39d","tree_id":"e2e469d9f72295881ebefd3f996d62fa9e91c498","timestamp":"2026-08-06T12:46:28Z","committer":{"name":"stian-sandvold","email":"stian@dhis2.org"}},"workflow_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/workflows/10954","repository":{"id":66940520,"node_id":"MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnk2Njk0MDUyMA==","owner":{"login":"dhis2","id":1089987,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjEwO